<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dalia Grybauskaitė</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1956</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dalia Grybauskaitė is a Lithuanian politician who was president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> from 2009 to 2019, the first woman in the office and the first to be re-elected for a second consecutive term. An economist, she previously served as finance minister and as European Commissioner for Financial Programming and the Budget from 2004 to 2009. She was known for her firm opposition to Russian policy, especially after 2014.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dalia-grybauskaite.jpg" alt="Dalia Grybauskaitė" width="320" height="397" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Algirdas Gataveckas · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dalia_Grybauskait%C4%97_(2019).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
